    turnFlow: 'Lead is by lot in the first hand and then rotates. Opening lead must be a double or a scoring starter tile such as 0-5, 1-4, 2-3, 4-6, or 5-5; if unavailable, lead passes onward. Players match open ends or pass if blocked. Any scoring play or any double gives an immediate extra turn. If a player uses their last tile on a scoring play or double, they are washed up and play continues among others. A hand ends when a player dominoes on a non-scoring non-double play, or when the game blocks.',
